  "courseName": "Introduction to Astronomy",
  "estimatedLength": "35 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Describe apparent retrograde motion and how outer planets like Mars periodically appear to reverse direction against the background stars",
    "Explain how the geocentric model required epicycles to account for retrograde loops",
    "Demonstrate how the heliocentric model naturally produces retrograde motion through the relative orbital motion of Earth and an outer planet",
    "Compare the retrograde behavior of Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn and relate differences to their distance from the Sun"
