                    255,
                    255
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 36
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Mars completes the loop and resumes eastward motion, completing the full retrograde event and posing the central question.",
          "narration": "Finally Mars slows again, reverses once more, and resumes its eastward march. This looping reversal repeats roughly every twenty-six months. For centuries, the question was simple but profound: why would a planet move backward?"
        }
