          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Delivers the passing-car analogy and ties the overtaking moment directly to the observed retrograde loop.",
          "narration": "This is exactly like passing a slower car on the highway. As you overtake it, the other car seems to drift backward, even though both of you are moving forward. When Earth overtakes Mars, Mars appears to loop backward against the stars. The retrograde loop falls out naturally, no epicycles required."
        }
